  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Parle Agro Private Limited Others & Ors vs The Municipal Corporation Delhi on 23 March, 2026 Author: Amit Bansal Bench: Amit Bansal $~18 * In The High Court Of Delhi At New Delhi + W.P.(C) 2568/2023 & Cm Appl. 9816/2023 Parle Agro Private Limited Others & Ors. .....Petitio Through: Mr. Rajiv Tyagi, Mr. Rahul Tya Mr. Rohit Gupta, Advocates. versus The Municipal Corporation Delhi ..... Respond Through: Ms. Beenashaw N. Soni, Sc for with Ms. Ann Joseph and Ms. Ma Jain, Advocates. Mr. Amit Meharia, Ms. Tannisth Singh and Mr. Shashwat Roy, Advocates for R-2 / Fssai. Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Amit Bansal Order",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Mr. Rajiv Tyagi, counsel appearing on behalf of the petitioner submits that since the petitioner company has the requisite licenses under the provisions of The Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (FSSAI Act), no municipal license would be required. Ms. Beenashaw N. Soni, counsel appearing on behalf of the respondent no.1/MCD submits that since the activity carried out by the petitioner falls within the ambit of activities mentioned in Schedule 11 read with Section 417 of the DMC Act, the petitioner would be required to take the municipal license.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Mr. Rajiv Tyagi, counsel appearing on behalf of the petitioner submits that since the petitioner company has the requisite licenses under the provisions of The Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (FSSAI Act), no municipal license would be required. Ms. Beenashaw N. Soni, counsel appearing on behalf of the respondent no.1/MCD submits that since the activity carried out by the petitioner falls within the ambit of activities mentioned in Schedule 11 read with Section 417 of the DMC Act, the petitioner would be required to take the municipal license.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
